{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.coloredJones41_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.coloredJones41_two","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroNewtonLadder.lean#L225-L234","doc":"**Anchor**: `J_2` is the Jones polynomial of the figure-eight,\n`V(4₁) = q² + q⁻² − q − q⁻¹ + 1` (the same anchor the compute uses). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.coloredJones41_bar_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.coloredJones41_bar_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroNewtonLadder.lean#L215-L223","doc":"**Bar symmetry / amphichirality, all `N`**: `J_N(4₁; q⁻¹) = J_N(4₁; q)`\n— manifest from the Λ-Newton form since every node is bar-even (the\nprobe's empirical check for `N ≤ 9`, now structural). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.coloredJones41_sum_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.coloredJones41_sum_stable","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroNewtonLadder.lean#L205-L213","doc":"**Termination, all `N ≥ 1`**: extending the Newton sum past `k = N − 1`\nchanges nothing — the `j = N` factor is `λ_N − λ_N = 0` (the probe's\ncheck for `N ≤ 6`, now structural). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.coloredJones41_eq_newton_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.coloredJones41_eq_newton_sum","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroNewtonLadder.lean#L197-L203","doc":"**Main identity (Λ-Newton / cyclotomic form), all `N`**:\n`J_N(4₁; q) = ∑_{k<N} ∏_{j=1}^{k} (Λ_N − λ_j)` with `Λ_N = λ_N` — all\nHabiro cyclotomic coefficients equal 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.coloredJones41","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.coloredJones41","kind":"def","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroNewtonLadder.lean#L191-L195","doc":"The N-colored Jones polynomial of the figure-eight knot `4₁`\n(Habiro–Lê form, normalized `J_1 = 1`), as used by\n`computations/figure_eight_aj_operator.py`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.habiroTerm_eq_newtonLadder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.habiroTerm_eq_newtonLadder","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroNewtonLadder.lean#L174-L189","doc":"**Termwise Habiro ↔ Newton identity** (strictly stronger than the summed\nprobe check): each Habiro–Lê summand IS the Newton-ladder element on the\nbar-even nodes, evaluated at `x = λ_N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.habiro_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.habiro_factor","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroNewtonLadder.lean#L162-L172","doc":"Per-factor identity:\n`q^N (1 − q^{−N−1−j})(1 − q^{j+1−N}) = λ_N − λ_{j+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.habiroTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.habiroTerm","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroNewtonLadder.lean#L155-L160","doc":"The Habiro–Lê summand of the figure-eight colored Jones:\n`q^{Nk} · (q^{−N−1}; q^{−1})_k · (q^{−N+1}; q)_k`, with the two\nq-Pochhammer products written inverse-explicitly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.multiplier_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.multiplier_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroNewtonLadder.lean#L148-L153","doc":"**The ladder multiplier `A_k = x − λ_{k+1}` is bar-even** (for any\nbar-fixed `x`) — the shape requirement of the 1jrh one-recurrence\nhypothesis, satisfied on the proved knot side. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.lam_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.lam_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroNewtonLadder.lean#L143-L146","doc":"**Nodes are bar-even**: `λ_j(q⁻¹) = λ_j(q)`.  Holds unconditionally over\na field (`0⁻¹ = 0` covers `q = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.lam","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.lam","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroNewtonLadder.lean#L140-L141","doc":"The bar-even node `λ_j = q^j + q^{−j}` (written inverse-explicitly). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.newtonLadder_sum_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.newtonLadder_sum_stable","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroNewtonLadder.lean#L119-L131","doc":"**Generalized sum truncation**: the ladder sum is stable under extending\nthe range past the hit node — the 4₁ mechanism `Λ_N = λ_N` in general\nform. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.newtonLadder_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.newtonLadder_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroNewtonLadder.lean#L110-L117","doc":"**Generalized termination**: once the evaluation point hits a node\n(`x = a m`, `1 ≤ m`), every ladder element of index `≥ m` vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.newtonLadder_casoratian_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.newtonLadder_casoratian_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroNewtonLadder.lean#L102-L108","doc":"The Newton ladder is itself such a first-order ladder, so its Casoratian\nagainst any other solution of the same ladder vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.casoratian_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.casoratian_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroNewtonLadder.lean#L91-L100","doc":"**Generalized Casoratian collapse.**  Over any commutative ring, any two\nsolutions of a first-order (two-term) ladder `u_{k+1} = A_k u_k` have\nidentically vanishing Casoratian (discrete Wronskian).  This is the\nstructural reason a `B_k ≡ 0` ladder carries no Casoratian sign\ninformation for the 1jrh Askey–Wilson test. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.newtonLadder_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.newtonLadder_succ","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroNewtonLadder.lean#L81-L89","doc":"**The ladder is two-term (first-order): `B_k ≡ 0`.**  In the normal form\n`g_{k+1} = A_k g_k + B_k g_{k−1}` the multiplier is `A_k = x − a (k+1)`\nand the lower coefficient vanishes identically — the degenerate\nNewton-interpolation boundary of the Askey–Wilson three-term shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.newtonLadder_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.newtonLadder_zero","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroNewtonLadder.lean#L77-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.newtonLadder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder.newtonLadder","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroNewtonLadder.lean#L72-L75","doc":"Newton-interpolation ladder on the nodes `a 1, a 2, …`:\n`g_k(x) = ∏_{j=1}^{k} (x − a j)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}